```text
HEAD:
var full = Math.abs(e[u] - s[u]) < 1e-5 && Math.abs(e[v] - s[v]) < 1e-5;
if (!full) full = _arcSweep(a, u, v) > Math.PI;

upstream/main:
var full = e[u] === s[u] && e[v] === s[v];
if (!full) {
  var a0 = Math.atan2(s[v] - c[v], s[u] - c[u]), a1 = Math.atan2(e[v] - c[v], e[u] - c[u]);
  var sweep = a.ccw ? a1 - a0 : a0 - a1;
  if (sweep < 0) sweep += 2 * Math.PI;
  full = sweep > Math.PI;
}
```

Both branches change the same logic. The author-side conflict instruction requires a stop. I aborted the merge.
The worktree is clean and remains in place. No commit or push occurred. No label changed.

